<!--
    Return-flow regression for `option msvcstackguard`.  The caller has two
    semantic return values which join at one `/GS` epilogue:

        2000  sub  rsp,0x48
              mov  rax,[cookie]
              xor  rax,rsp
              mov  [rsp+0x38],rax
              test ecx,ecx
              jne  failure
              call success_side_effect
              xor  eax,eax              ; success: EAX = 0
              jmp  shared
        failure:
              call failure_side_effect
              mov  eax,1                ; failure: EAX = 1
        shared:
              mov  rcx,[rsp+0x38]
              xor  rcx,rsp              ; (K ^ SP) ^ SP
        2032  call 2100                 ; checker
              add  rsp,0x48
              ret

    The checker is deliberately unnamed.  Its failure tail enters 0x2130,
    whose ordinary returning CALL at 0x2134 precedes INT 0x29.  That nested
    call makes the generic callee-body write probe incomplete; the option must
    rely only on its exact `(K ^ SP) ^ SP`, one-direct-call recognition seed.

    Four passes cross `msvcstackguard` with `calleeretpreserves`.  With the
    former OFF, both latter settings retain exactly the raw checker call and
    cookie algebra.  With it ON, both settings remove the boilerplate and keep
    the two machine return values (canonically rendered as `a0 != 0`).  The two
    arm-specific calls keep the control-flow split observable.  This pins the
    option-owned P7-to-P3 restart handoff independently of the generic
    return-preservation heuristic.
-->
